**Email forwarding can be useful, but can also pose a security risk due to the potential disclosure of information.**
<br>

Users can configure [<b>Inbox rules</b>](https://support.microsoft.com/en-US/Outlook/mail/use-rules-to-automatically-forward-messages) in Outlook or set up [<b>SMTP forwarding</b>](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/turn-on-automatic-forwarding-in-outlook-7f2670a1-7fff-4475-8a3c-5822d63b0c8e) to automatically forward messages to external recipients. You can control automatic external email forwarding from cloud mailboxes using [<b>Outbound spam policies</b>](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-office-365/outbound-spam-policies-external-email-forwarding) in Microsoft Defender for Office 365. 
**Attackers might exploit this capability to compromise your organization or its partners.**<br><br>**Recommended action:** Investigate external auto-forwarding - it is a common data-exfiltration path. Consider disabling auto-forwarding via the outbound spam policy unless a business case is documented."},"name":"text - 8","id":"b04d1590-98e3-4650-9172-33e75561e1e5"},{"type":1,"content":{"json":"### Automatic Email Forwarding by Type<br>

